<title>USA: Brownlee 235 MW unit shut for planned maintenance.</title>
<headline>Brownlee 235 MW unit shut for planned maintenance.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 235 megawatt (MW) unit 5 at the Brownlee hydropower project on the Snake River in Idaho was shut Monday for planned maintenance, sources familiar with the project's operations said.</p>
<p>The turbine unit was expected to be out of service for 40 days.</p>
<p>Other turbines at Brownlee, which has a nameplate capacity of 5,854 MW, were said to be operating normally.</p>
<p>The hydropower project is owned and operated by Idaho Power Co.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
</text>
